4
00:00:08.313 --> 00:00:09.487
What this tab is.

5
00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:28.583
These are end-to-end system designs for real sectors, each in the handbook's 9-part format: requirements and estimates;. architecture with happy-path and failure-path diagrams;. a design-doc excerpt;. four runnable labs with recorded outputs;. production concerns and anti-patterns;.

6
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:31.469
20 interview questions.

7
00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:35.354
Each design builds on the core chapters rather than repeating them.

8
00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:40.157
From I04 onwards the designs are system walkthroughs with no code.

9
00:00:40.437 --> 00:00:49.354
They explain in detail how the system works end to end: journeys, subsystems, algorithms, the data platform and warehouse, and the tech stack.

10
00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:57.421
I01 and I02 have companion walkthrough pages (I01b, I02b) in the same style.

11
00:00:57.701 --> 00:01:01.882
Company-named designs are in the style of and based on public sources.

12
00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:05.362
They are not descriptions of any company's internal systems.

13
00:01:05.642 --> 00:01:08.266
Regulatory statements are marked VERIFY.

